      },
      "message": "fix(slot): cut the round ends of a slot wider than the tool\n\nA row of a wide Slot touches each round end only at its end point. The\ntool did not follow the arc between two row ends and left up to 0.86 mm\non the wall (10 mm slot, 6 mm tool), and verify passed it.\n\nAfter the rows, each level now runs one lap of the cutter-centre stadium\nfrom the last row's end: two straight sides and two half circles, each\nhalf circle as two quarter arcs. The lap is counterclockwise under climb\nand clockwise otherwise. A full-width slot (h = 0) is unchanged.\n\nGoldens: slot_wide_channel_rows (CL and each NC dialect) gain the six lap\nmoves for each level; the catalog case 2d/slots is rebuilt.\n\nFixes #2906\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
